    LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING
    FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER
    DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.

    qore#5819: the HTTP/2 server took all the output of nghttp2 into its send buffer whether or not the socket could
    take it, so the data held for a peer that does not read was limited only by the flow-control window that the
    peer grants.  The output is now taken only up to a high-water mark of unwritten data, and the rest stays in the
    streams' pending data, where the per-stream limits apply.
*/

%modern

%prepend-module-path "${SCRIPT_DIR}/../../../../qlib"
%requires Util
%requires QUnit
%requires Logger
%requires HttpServerUtil
%requires AsyncSocketIo
%requires HttpServerAsyncIo
%requires HttpServer
%requires ServerSentEventHandler
%requires HttpClientIo

%exec-class Http2SendBufferBoundTest

#! The bound on every blocking wait in this test: a hang guard only, never a timing assertion
const HangGuard = 60s;

#! The size of each write
const ChunkSize = 32768;

#! The data written to the non-reading peer before its stream must report a full buffer (a hang guard: 256 MiB)
const MaxBytes = 256 * 1024 * 1024;

#! The body size of the large response
const BigBody = 8 * 1024 * 1024;

